(RADIOLOGY REPORT - MRI RIGHT KNEE WITHOUT CONTRAST) Tj
(CLINICAL HISTORY: 24-year-old recreational soccer player with acute right) '
(knee injury sustained during a pivoting maneuver three days ago. Positive) '
(Lachman and pivot-shift tests on exam.) '
(FINDINGS: Complete full-thickness tear of the anterior cruciate ligament) '
(\(ACL\) with associated bone marrow edema at the lateral femoral condyle and) '
(posterior lateral tibial plateau. Menisci are intact. No evidence of) '
(collateral ligament injury or chondral defect.) '
(IMPRESSION: Complete ACL rupture, right knee. Findings are consistent with) '
(the clinical diagnosis of ACL reconstruction candidacy. Recommend) '
(orthopedic surgery referral for operative planning.) '
